[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Time Series Specific Operations in MongoDB"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"MongoDB provides specific operations and features designed to efficiently handle time series data. These operations are optimized for storing, querying, and analyzing data that changes over time. This tutorial covers key time series specific operations in MongoDB."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Creating Time Series Collections"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To work with time series data, you first need to create a time series collection. This is done using the 'createCollection' command with specific options."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"db.createCollection("sensorData", {
  timeField: "timestamp",
  metaField: "metadata",
  granularity: "seconds"
})"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"In the above example:
- 'sensorData' is the name of the collection.
- 'timeField' specifies the field that contains the timestamp values (in this case, 'timestamp').
- 'metaField' specifies the field that contains metadata associated with the time series (in this case, 'metadata').
- 'granularity' specifies the expected interval between data points ('seconds', 'minutes', 'hours')."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Inserting Time Series Data"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Inserting data into a time series collection is similar to inserting into a regular collection, but the documents must conform to the structure defined during collection creation."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"db.sensorData.insertOne({
  timestamp: new Date(),
  metadata: { sensorId: "S123", location: "Room 101" },
  temperature: 25.5,
  humidity: 60
})"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Each document contains the 'timestamp', 'metadata', and the actual time series data ('temperature', 'humidity')."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Querying Time Series Data"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can query time series data using standard MongoDB query operators, taking advantage of the indexed 'timeField'."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"// Find all data points within a specific time range
db.sensorData.find({
  timestamp: {
    $gte: new Date("2023-01-01T00:00:00Z"),
    $lt: new Date("2023-01-02T00:00:00Z")
  }
}).toArray()"},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"// Find data points for a specific sensor
db.sensorData.find({
  "metadata.sensorId": "S123"
}).toArray()"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Time Series Aggregations"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"MongoDB's aggregation framework is powerful for analyzing time series data. You can perform calculations, group data by time intervals, and identify trends."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"// Calculate the average temperature per hour
db.sensorData.aggregate([
  {
    $match: {
      "metadata.sensorId": "S123"
    }
  },
  {
    $group: {
      _id: {
        $dateTrunc: {
          date: "$timestamp",
          unit: "hour"
        }
      },
      avgTemperature: { $avg: "$temperature" }
    }
  },
  {
    $sort: { _id: 1 }
  }
]).toArray()"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"This example uses '$dateTrunc' to group data by hour and calculates the average temperature for each hour."},{"order":19,"type":"subheading","text":"Data Expiration (TTL Indexes)"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"To automatically remove old time series data, you can use TTL (Time-To-Live) indexes. This ensures that your collection doesn't grow indefinitely."},{"order":21,"type":"code","text":"// Create a TTL index to remove data older than 30 days
db.sensorData.createIndex(
  { timestamp: 1 },
  { expireAfterSeconds: 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 }
)"},{"order":22,"type":"paragraph","text":"This index will automatically delete documents where the 'timestamp' field is older than 30 days."},{"order":23,"type":"subheading","text":"Considerations"},{"order":24,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Choose the appropriate 'granularity' based on your data frequency. Incorrect granularity can impact performance."},{"order":25,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure the 'timeField' is properly indexed for efficient querying."},{"order":26,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use the aggregation framework for complex analysis and reporting on time series data."},{"order":27,"type":"paragraph","text":"By leveraging these time series specific operations, you can effectively manage and analyze time-based data in MongoDB."}]
